{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via a cobbler orchestrator system) has assigned Task #5368: `[stitch] srd041-id R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1`. The task requires implementing the `id` utility in Go with two files:\n   - `cmd/id/main.go` — the id utility with core user/group identity printing\n   - `cmd/id/id_test.go` — differential tests against `gid` reference binary\n   \n   Only four specific requirements from srd041-id are in scope:\n   - **R1.1**: Default output format: `uid=N(name) gid=N(name) groups=N(name),N(name),...` followed by newline\n   - **R1.2**: Groups list must include all supplementary groups in system order\n   - **R1.3**: Exit 0 on success\n   - **R2.1**: `-u` or `--user` flag prints only the effective UID (numeric by default)\n   \n   Requirements R2.2, R2.3, R2.4, R3.x are explicitly NOT in scope for this task.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `id` utility verified via differential testing\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary` for differential testing framework\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - Homebrew g-prefix convention: reference binary is `gid`\n   - `exec.LookPath` + `t.Skip` pattern for graceful test skip when reference binary missing\n   - Go's `os/user` package for user/group lookups\n   - `os.Getuid()`, `os.Getgid()` for effective UID/GID\n   - `os/user.LookupId()`, `os/user.LookupGroupId()` for name resolution\n   - `os/user.Current()` and group membership APIs\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - 40-line function size hard limit\n   - 500-line file size limit\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n   - Write all files before building/testing (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd041-id.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD defining the id utility requirements\n     - R1 (Default output): R1.1 format string, R1.2 group ordering, R1.3 exit code\n     - R2 (Selection flags): R2.1 (-u/--user), R2.2 (-g/--group), R2.3 (-G/--groups), R2.4 (mutual exclusion)\n     - R3 (Modifier flags): R3.1 (-n/--name), R3.2 (-r/--real), R3.3 (USER operand)\n     - R4 (Differential testing): R4.1-R4.3 test requirements\n     - Non-goals: No -Z/--context (SELinux), no -p (BSD), no NIS/LDAP beyond NSS\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (provided inline in prompt)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function that sets up SIGPIPE handler for exit 0\n     - Must be called at start of main()\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (provided inline)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd/ package and returns binary path\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided inline)\n     - `DiffTest` struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode, etc.\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs differential tests\n     - Harness sets LC_ALL=C by default\n   \n   - **cmd/id/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - id utility implementing R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\n   \n   - **cmd/id/id_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests against gid for the four requirements\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only one tool call (Read) was made before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand exact requirements before implementation\n   - Identified that only R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1 are in scope (not R2.2-R4.3)\n   - No implementation has been done yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Massive task prompt with full project context, task description for #5368 ([stitch] srd041-id R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1), execution constitution, coding standards, shared protocols, package contracts, and all inline source code