{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014SE2VWBvDys1TuUhURGvJb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// Implements srd042-whoami R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"fmt\"\n9\t\t\"os\"\n10\t\t\"os/user\"\n11\t\t\"strings\"\n12\t\n13\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n14\t)\n15\t\n16\tconst helpText = `Usage: whoami [OPTION]...\n17\tPrint the user name associated with the current effective user ID.\n18\tSame as id -un.\n19\t\n20\t      --help     display this help and exit\n21\t      --version  output version information and exit\n22\t`\n23\t\n24\tconst versionText = `whoami (go-unix-utils) dev\n25\t`\n26\t\n27\tfunc main() {\n28\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n29\t\targs := os.Args[1:]\n30\t\targs = parseFlags(args)\n31\t\n32\t\tif len(args) > 0 {\n33\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n34\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'whoami --help' for more information.\")\n35\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n36\t\t}\n37\t\n38\t\tu, err := user.Current()\n39\t\tif err != nil {\n40\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: cannot find name for user ID %d: %v\\n\", os.Geteuid(), err)\n41\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n42\t\t}\n43\t\n44\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, u.Username); err != nil {\n45\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n46\t\t}\n47\t}\n48\t\n49\tfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n50\t\tfor len(args) > 0 {\n51\t\t\tswitch args[0] {\n52\t\t\tcase \"--help\":\n53\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n54\t\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n55\t\t\tcase \"--version\":\n56\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n57\t\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n58\t\t\tcase \"--\":\n59\t\t\t\treturn args[1:]\n60\t\t\tdefault:\n61\t\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n62\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n63\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'whoami --help' for more information.\")\n64\t\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n65\t\t\t\t}\n66\t\t\t\treturn args\n67\t\t\t}\n68\t\t}\n69\t\treturn args\n70\t}\n71\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkKc6Hq3VdpAVG4VwB4SWJ","session_id":"aa3fee76-1f98-465b-9d3b-deb0828dedfd","uuid":"25dd23aa-1582-4387-9c65-d4f395dca6fc","timestamp":"2026-05-20T14:28:16.258Z"}
